<title>GERMANY: Bayer settles U.S. dispute with Barr.</title>
<headline>Bayer settles U.S. dispute with Barr.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group Bayer AG said Friday it and its U.S. subsidiary Bayer Corporation reached an agreement with Barr Laboratories Inc. to end litigation over the U.S. patent on Ciprofloxacin.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Barr, a maker of generic drugs, acknowledges the validity of Bayer's worldwide patents on Ciprofloxacin, an ingredient that fights infections, Bayer said. As part of the pact, Bayer will pay $24.5 million in 1997 to both Barr and Rugby Laboratories Inc., which has supported Barr during the dispute.</p>
<p>Ciprofloxacin is used to treat lower respiratory, skin, bone and joint, and urinary tract infections.</p>
